  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "SQRT is rounded twice, once to 64 bits and once to 53",
  "statement": "The worksheet SQRT is RN53(RN64(sqrt(x))): the root is rounded to the x87 unit's 64-bit significand and then stored to binary64. On inputs where that double rounding lands differently from a single rounding, Excel takes the double-rounded value: SQRT(0.9999999999999999) is 1. The smallest subnormal input returns 0.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "41,897 of 41,897 distinct normal positive bank rows match. On the 164 rows where double and correct rounding differ, Excel follows double rounding every time. The subnormal result rests on 1 row.",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": null,
